IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `jccv-core`

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) -- THE PARTY'S SEAT: the person bringing a civil claim (or
-- answering one) whose proceeding may be in, or may move between, the Supreme Court of South Australia, another State's
-- or Territory's Supreme Court, the Federal Court and the Family Court. Every question is asked as that person would ask
-- it, from facts that person can state; the courts' opinions are asked as conditions ("the court finds ..."). The rules
-- are in jccv-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (version of 4 September 2006, fetched 6 November
-- 2026). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The party's questions`

§§ `Does the scheme reach my case (ss 3, 3A, 4)`

@export Does the South Australian cross-vesting scheme cover my proceeding at all (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 3(1), 3A, 4(5))?
GIVEN `it is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is a criminal prosecution (a civil claim for damages or compensation is not)
      `it is a Corporations Act matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the jurisdiction concerned is the jurisdiction in civil matters under the Corporations legislation that Division 1 of Part 9.6A of the Corporations Act 2001 (Cth) deals with
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`Does the cross-vesting scheme cover my proceeding` MEANS
    `does the Act cover the proceeding (ss 3(1), 3A, 4(5))` `it is criminal` `it is a Corporations Act matter`

@export Can a court outside South Australia hear my South Australian claim, a "State matter" (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 3(1), 4)?
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court` @desc The court you are asking about: the Supreme Court of South Australia; another South Australian court; the Supreme Court of another State, the Northern Territory or the ACT; the Supreme Court of an external Territory (such as Norfolk Island); the Family Court of Western Australia (a State Family Court); the Federal Court; the Family Court of Australia; or another court or tribunal
      `the SA Supreme Court could hear it under SA law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court of South Australia has jurisdiction in your matter otherwise than because of a law of the Commonwealth or of another State (for example a claim in negligence, contract or under a South Australian Act)
      `it was removed into the SA Supreme Court under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your matter was removed into the Supreme Court of South Australia from a lower court or tribunal by an order under s 8
      `it is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a criminal matter
      `it is a Corporations Act matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is jurisdiction dealt with by Division 1 of Part 9.6A of the Corporations Act 2001 (Cth)
GIVETH A `State matter jurisdiction answer`
`Can that court hear my South Australian claim` MEANS
    `may that court hear the State matter (s 4)` `the court` (`is a State matter (s 3(1))` `the SA Supreme Court could hear it under SA law` `it was removed into the SA Supreme Court under s 8`) `it is criminal` `it is a Corporations Act matter`

§§ `Will my proceeding be transferred (s 5)`
-- Situation: your proceeding is pending in one of the courts and a transfer has been raised, by a party, an
-- Attorney-General or the court itself.

@export My proceeding is in the Supreme Court of South Australia: must it be transferred to the Federal Court or the Family Court (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 5(1), 6A(4))?
GIVEN `the court finds the federal court more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Supreme Court, having regard to whether the proceeding could only have been brought in the Federal Court or the Family Court, how far it turns on Commonwealth law outside the Supreme Court's own jurisdiction, and the interests of justice, that it is more appropriate for that court to decide it
      `which court` IS A `Federal court` @desc Which court the Supreme Court considers more appropriate: the Federal Court or the Family Court
      `it is a federal matter proceeding with a related State proceeding in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is a "federal matter proceeding" under s 6A (a Commonwealth body acting under a South Australian law) whose related State matter proceeding is pending in a South Australian court (usually no)
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`Must my SA Supreme Court proceeding go to the Federal Court or Family Court` MEANS
    `transfer to the Federal Court or Family Court (s 5(1))` `the court finds the federal court more appropriate` `which court` `it is a federal matter proceeding with a related State proceeding in SA`

@export My proceeding is in the Supreme Court of South Australia: must it be transferred to the Supreme Court of another State or Territory (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 5(2))?
GIVEN `the court finds it related to a proceeding there and more appropriate there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the court that your proceeding arises out of, or is related to, a proceeding pending in the other Supreme Court, and that court is the more appropriate one
      `the court finds the other court more appropriate on the factors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the court, having regard to whether it could only have been brought in the other State, how far it turns on that State's law, and the interests of justice, that the other Supreme Court is more appropriate
      `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the court that it is otherwise in the interests of justice for the other Supreme Court to decide it
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`Must my SA Supreme Court proceeding go to another Supreme Court` MEANS
    `transfer to another Supreme Court (s 5(2))` `the court finds it related to a proceeding there and more appropriate there` `the court finds the other court more appropriate on the factors` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice`

@export My proceeding is in the Supreme Court of another State or Territory: must it be transferred to the Supreme Court of South Australia (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 5(3))?
GIVEN `the court finds it related to a proceeding in SA and SA more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to that court that your proceeding arises out of, or is related to, a proceeding pending in the Supreme Court of South Australia, and that court is the more appropriate one
      `the court finds SA more appropriate on the factors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to that court, having regard to whether it could only have been brought in South Australia, how far it turns on South Australian law, and the interests of justice, that the Supreme Court of South Australia is more appropriate
      `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to that court that it is otherwise in the interests of justice for the Supreme Court of South Australia to decide it
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`Must my proceeding come to the SA Supreme Court from another Supreme Court` MEANS
    `transfer to the Supreme Court of South Australia from another Supreme Court (s 5(3))` `the court finds it related to a proceeding in SA and SA more appropriate` `the court finds SA more appropriate on the factors` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice`

@export My proceeding is in the Federal Court or the Family Court: must it be transferred to the Supreme Court of South Australia (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 5(4), 6A(2), (3))?
GIVEN `it is a federal matter proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is a "federal matter proceeding" under s 6A (a Commonwealth body acting under a South Australian law, with a related State proceeding in a South Australian court) (usually no)
      `the court finds it related to a proceeding in SA and SA more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Federal Court or Family Court that your proceeding arises out of, or is related to, a proceeding pending in the Supreme Court of South Australia, and that court is the more appropriate one
      `the court finds SA more appropriate on the factors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to that court, having regard to whether it could not have been brought there but could in the Supreme Court, how far it turns on South Australian law, and the interests of justice, that the Supreme Court is more appropriate
      `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to that court that it is otherwise in the interests of justice for the Supreme Court of South Australia to decide it
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`Must my proceeding come to the SA Supreme Court from the Federal Court or Family Court` MEANS
    `transfer to the Supreme Court of South Australia from the Federal Court or Family Court (s 5(4))` `it is a federal matter proceeding` `the court finds it related to a proceeding in SA and SA more appropriate` `the court finds SA more appropriate on the factors` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice`

@export Another proceeding of mine (or related to mine) has been transferred: must my proceeding follow it to the same court (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 5(6))?
GIVEN `the other proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has transferred the other proceeding to another court under a cross-vesting law (of South Australia, the Commonwealth or another State)
      `mine is related and pending in that court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is pending in the same court and arises out of, or is related to, the transferred proceeding
      `the court finds the interests of justice favour the other court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the court that it is in the interests of justice for the other court to decide your proceeding too
GIVETH A `Related transfer answer`
`Must my related proceeding follow the transferred one` MEANS
    `must the related proceeding follow (s 5(6))` `the other proceeding was transferred under a cross-vesting law` `mine is related and pending in that court` `the court finds the interests of justice favour the other court`

@export Can I ask the court to transfer my proceeding under the cross-vesting scheme (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 3(1), 5(7))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who you are in the proceeding: a party to it; a person who has intervened in it; the Attorney-General of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or someone else
GIVETH A `Who may apply answer`
`Can I apply for a transfer` MEANS
    `who may apply for a transfer (s 5(7))` `who I am`

@export If my proceeding is transferred, can my lawyer keep acting for me in the new court (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 5(8))?
GIVEN `my lawyer may practise in the old court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lawyer is entitled to practise as a barrister, a solicitor or both in the court your proceeding was transferred from
      `it is the transferred proceeding or one heard with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the question is about the transferred proceeding itself, or another proceeding it arises out of or is related to that is to be decided together with it
GIVETH A `Right to practise answer`
`Can my lawyer act in the new court` MEANS
    `may the lawyer practise in the new court (s 5(8))` `my lawyer may practise in the old court` `it is the transferred proceeding or one heard with it`

§§ `Special federal matters (ss 6, 6A)`
-- Situation: your proceeding in the Supreme Court of South Australia includes a "special federal matter" (a matter the
-- Commonwealth Act reserves for the Federal Court or the Family Court), or a Commonwealth body acting under a South
-- Australian law is involved.

@export My proceeding in the Supreme Court of South Australia includes a special federal matter: must it be transferred, and to which court (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 6, 6A(4))?
GIVEN `the special federal matter` IS A `Special federal matter` @desc Whether a matter for decision is a special federal matter under s 3(1) of the Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Cth), and under which paragraph: none; paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) (Federal Court matters); or paragraph (ab) (family law matters)
      `it is an appeal and the trial court kept the matter under s 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is an appeal instituted in the Full Court of the Supreme Court from a court that had ordered under s 6(3) that it would decide the special federal matter itself
      `the court has ordered that it keep the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has made an order under s 6(3) that it decide the proceeding itself
      `it is a federal matter proceeding with a related State proceeding in SA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is a "federal matter proceeding" under s 6A whose related State matter proceeding is pending in a South Australian court (usually no)
GIVETH A `Special federal matter answer`
`Must my special federal matter be transferred` MEANS
    `must the special federal matter be transferred (s 6)` `the special federal matter` `it is an appeal and the trial court kept the matter under s 6(3)` `the court has ordered that it keep the proceeding` `it is a federal matter proceeding with a related State proceeding in SA`

@export Can the Supreme Court of South Australia keep my special federal matter and decide it itself (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 6(3)-(6))?
GIVEN `the court is satisfied there are special reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court is satisfied that there are special reasons, in the particular circumstances of your proceeding, for it to decide the proceeding (having regard to the general rule that special federal matters go to the Federal Court or the Family Court, and any Attorney-General's submission)
      `the only reasons are the parties' convenience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reasons put are ones relevant to the convenience of the parties (cost, distance, the lawyers already engaged)
      `notice has gone to both Attorneys-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written notice of the nature of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth Attorney-General and the South Australian Attorney-General
      `a reasonable time has passed since the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable time has passed since the notice for the Attorneys-General to consider making submissions
GIVETH A `Keep order answer`
`Can the SA Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` MEANS
    `may the Supreme Court keep the special federal matter (s 6(3)-(5))` `the court is satisfied there are special reasons` `the only reasons are the parties' convenience` `notice has gone to both Attorneys-General` `a reasonable time has passed since the notice`

@export While my special federal matter waits to be transferred, can I still get urgent interim orders from the Supreme Court of South Australia (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 6(7))?
GIVEN `the relief is urgent and interlocutory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief you seek is urgent and of an interlocutory (interim) nature, such as an injunction until the hearing
      `the court finds it in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds that granting it is in the interests of justice
GIVETH A `Urgent relief answer`
`Can I get urgent interim relief meanwhile` MEANS
    `may urgent relief be granted meanwhile (s 6(7))` `the relief is urgent and interlocutory` `the court finds it in the interests of justice`

@export Is my proceeding a "federal matter proceeding" (a Commonwealth body acting under a South Australian law), and what follows (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 6A)?
GIVEN `it is a paragraph (c) or (e) special federal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a matter for decision falls under paragraph (c) or (e) of the definition of special federal matter in s 3(1) of the Commonwealth Act (judicial review-type matters)
      `it concerns a Commonwealth body acting under a State enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involves or relates to the exercise, or purported or proposed exercise, of functions or powers given to a Commonwealth authority or officer by a State enactment of the kind in paragraph (ca) or (cb) of the definition of enactment in the Administrative Decisions (Judicial Review) Act 1977 (Cth)
      `a related State matter proceeding is pending in an SA court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it arises out of, or relates to, another proceeding pending in any South Australian court (whichever began first)
      `that proceeding arises under the State enactment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other proceeding arises, wholly or substantially, under the State enactment or a corresponding enactment of another State
      `that proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether none of the matters in that other proceeding falls under paragraph (c) or (e) of the Commonwealth definition
      `where it is now` IS A `Court` @desc The court your proceeding is pending in now
GIVETH A `Federal matter proceeding answer`
`Is mine a federal matter proceeding and what follows` MEANS
    `what follows for a federal matter proceeding (s 6A)` (`is a federal matter proceeding (s 6A(1))` `it is a paragraph (c) or (e) special federal matter` `it concerns a Commonwealth body acting under a State enactment` `a related State matter proceeding is pending in an SA court` `that proceeding arises under the State enactment` `that proceeding has no paragraph (c) or (e) matter`) `where it is now`

@export The court decided my case although the Act said it should have gone elsewhere: is the decision invalid (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) ss 6(8), 7(7))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What went wrong` @desc What happened: the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order keeping it or the notice to the Attorneys-General, through inadvertence; the Full Court of the Supreme Court decided an appeal s 7(4) sends to the Federal or Family Court, because the interests of justice required it; the same, through inadvertence; or something else
GIVETH A `Validity answer`
`Is the decision in my case invalid` MEANS
    `is the decision invalidated (ss 6(8), 7(7))` `what happened`

§§ `Appeals (ss 7, 13)`
-- Situation: a decision has been given in your proceeding and you are thinking of appealing.

@export Where does my appeal go (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 7(1)-(5))?
GIVEN `the decision was by` IS A `Decision appealed from` @desc Who gave the decision you would appeal: a single judge of the Supreme Court of South Australia; a single judge of the Federal Court or the Family Court; a judge of a State Family Court; or another court
      `a matter arises under a Schedule Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a matter for decision in the appeal arises under an Act listed in the Schedule to the Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Cth) (federal Acts such as the Family Law Act 1975)
      `there is another matter too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appeal also involves a matter that does not arise under a Schedule Act
GIVETH AN `Appeal route answer`
`Where does my appeal go` MEANS
    `where does the appeal go (s 7)` `the decision was by` `a matter arises under a Schedule Act` `there is another matter too`

@export The Full Court of the Supreme Court of South Australia has begun hearing my appeal: will it send it to the Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 7(6), (7))?
GIVEN `the hearing has begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Full Court has begun to hear your appeal
      `it appears a Schedule Act matter is involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has since appeared to the Full Court that a matter in the appeal arises under a Schedule Act (so s 7(4) applies)
      `the court finds justice requires it to go on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Full Court finds that the interests of justice require it to go on and decide the appeal itself
GIVETH A `Full Court transfer answer`
`Will the Full Court send my appeal on` MEANS
    `will the Full Court send the appeal on (s 7(6))` `the hearing has begun` `it appears a Schedule Act matter is involved` `the court finds justice requires it to go on`

@export Can I appeal against the court's decision to transfer (or not to transfer) my proceeding, or its decision on which rules of evidence and procedure apply (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 13)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision` @desc Which decision: one about transferring or removing your proceeding under this Act; one on which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1); or another decision
GIVETH AN `Appeal bar answer`
`Can I appeal that decision` MEANS
    `can the decision be appealed (s 13)` `the decision`

§§ `Bringing a claim up from a lower court (ss 8, 10)`
-- Situation: your proceeding is in a lower South Australian court or a tribunal, or is a Trade Practices consumer
-- claim in a Supreme Court.

@export My proceeding is in a lower South Australian court or a tribunal: can it be removed into the Supreme Court of South Australia (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 8)?
GIVEN `where it is` IS A `Pending in` @desc Where your proceeding is pending: a South Australian court other than the Supreme Court; a tribunal established by or under an Act; or somewhere else
      `the Supreme Court finds it related to a proceeding elsewhere that could then come to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Supreme Court that your proceeding arises out of, or is related to, a proceeding in the Federal Court, the Family Court or another Supreme Court that could be transferred to the Supreme Court of South Australia if yours were removed
      `the Supreme Court finds removal needed to consider a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the Supreme Court that your proceeding should be removed so that it can consider transferring it to another court
GIVETH A `Removal answer`
`Can my proceeding be removed into the SA Supreme Court` MEANS
    `may the proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court (s 8)` `where it is` `the Supreme Court finds it related to a proceeding elsewhere that could then come to it` `the Supreme Court finds removal needed to consider a transfer`

@export My consumer claim under Division 1 or 1A of Part V of the Trade Practices Act 1974 is in a Supreme Court: can it be sent to a lower South Australian court (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 10)?
GIVEN `it is in a Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding is pending in the Supreme Court of South Australia or the Supreme Court of another State or a Territory
      `it is a TPA Part V Division 1 or 1A matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a matter in it arises under Division 1 (unfair practices) or 1A (product safety and information) of Part V of the Trade Practices Act 1974 (Cth)
      `it has a special federal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any matter in it is a special federal matter
      `it is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an appeal from a judgment of a court
      `a lower SA court has jurisdiction over all of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a South Australian court other than the Supreme Court (such as the District Court or Magistrates Court) has jurisdiction over all the matters in it
GIVETH A `Trade practices transfer answer`
`Can my Trade Practices claim go to a lower SA court` MEANS
    `may the Trade Practices matter go to a lower court (s 10)` `it is in a Supreme Court` `it is a TPA Part V Division 1 or 1A matter` `it has a special federal matter` `it is an appeal` `a lower SA court has jurisdiction over all of it`

§§ `After a transfer (ss 11, 12, 14)`
-- Situation: your proceeding is being heard in cross-vested jurisdiction, or has been transferred or removed.

@export Which law will the court apply to my claim when it is exercising cross-vested jurisdiction (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 11(1))?
GIVEN `the court is exercising cross-vested jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears to the court that, in deciding your matter, it will (or is likely to) be exercising jurisdiction given by this Act or another cross-vesting law
      `my right of action arises under another State's written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your right of action arises under a written law (an Act or regulation) of a State or Territory other than the one where the court is sitting
GIVETH A `Law applied answer`
`Which law applies to my claim` MEANS
    `which law will the court apply (s 11(1))` `the court is exercising cross-vested jurisdiction` `my right of action arises under another State's written law`

@export My proceeding has been transferred: do the steps and orders already made in the old court still count (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 11(3))?
GIVEN `it was transferred or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding has been transferred or removed to another court
      `the new court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new court has made an order that some earlier step does not count, or counts differently
GIVETH A `Steps answer`
`Do the steps already taken still count` MEANS
    `do the steps already taken count (s 11(3))` `it was transferred or removed` `the new court ordered otherwise`

@export My proceeding has been transferred: can the new court order costs for what happened before the transfer (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 12)?
GIVEN `it was transferred or removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceeding has been transferred or removed to another court
      `another court already dealt with those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs of the earlier part have already been dealt with by another court
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
`Can the new court order the earlier costs` MEANS
    `may the new court order the earlier costs (s 12)` `it was transferred or removed` `another court already dealt with those costs`

@export Can I enforce in South Australia a judgment of the Supreme Court of South Australia given in cross-vested jurisdiction (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 14(2))?
GIVEN `it is an SA Supreme Court judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment (a judgment, decree or order, final or interlocutory) is one of the Supreme Court of South Australia
      `it was given in cross-vested jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was given, wholly or partly, in jurisdiction conferred by a cross-vesting law
GIVETH AN `Enforcement answer`
`Can I enforce the judgment in South Australia` MEANS
    `is the judgment enforceable in South Australia (s 14(2))` `it is an SA Supreme Court judgment` `it was given in cross-vested jurisdiction`

@export A South Australian law refers to something done by the Supreme Court, and another court did it in cross-vested jurisdiction: does that count (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (SA) s 14(3))?
GIVEN `another court did it under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the thing was done by another court exercising jurisdiction conferred by this Act
      `the law is about enforcing judgments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the South Australian law that refers to the Supreme Court is a law relating to the enforcement of judgments
GIVETH A `Reference answer`
`Does the other court's act count under SA law` MEANS
    `does South Australian law treat it as done by the Supreme Court (s 14(3))` `another court did it under this Act` `the law is about enforcing judgments`
